=begin pod

=head1 NAME

Compress::Zlib::Raw - Low-level NativeCall bindings to zlib

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Low-level NativeCall bindings to zlib, with bundled zlib 1.4 libraries.

The package loads its own library from distribution resources. It does not
use a system zlib, download libraries, or compile code during installation.
Missing resources and unsupported platforms produce an error.

=head1 SUPPORTED PLATFORMS

=begin table
Platform         | Architectures  | Minimum runtime
=================|================|=================================
macOS            | x86-64, ARM64  | macOS 11
Windows          | x86-64, ARM64  | Windows with the Universal C Runtime
Linux with glibc | x86-64         | glibc 2.14
Linux with glibc | ARM64          | glibc 2.17
Linux with musl  | x86-64, ARM64  | See the bundled artifact manifest
=end table

Linux selects its libc variant from the running process's mapped loader.
It requires access to C</proc/self/maps>. Only 64-bit processes are supported.

Artifact origins, checksums, and build details are recorded in
L<resources/native-manifest.json|resources/native-manifest.json>.
The zlib license is included in
L<resources/licenses/zlib.txt|resources/licenses/zlib.txt>.

=head1 EXAMPLE

=begin code :lang<raku>
use v6;
use Compress::Zlib::Raw;
use NativeCall;

my $to-compress = 'test'.encode;
my $return-buf-len = CArray[long].new;
$return-buf-len[0] = 128;

my $return-buf = buf8.new;
$return-buf[127] = 0;

my $result = compress($return-buf, $return-buf-len, $to-compress, 4);
die if $result != Compress::Zlib::Raw::Z_OK;

my $orig-buf = buf8.new;
$orig-buf[127] = 1;

my $orig-size = CArray[long].new;
$orig-size[0] = 128;

$result = uncompress($orig-buf, $orig-size, $return-buf, $return-buf-len[0]);
die if $result != Compress::Zlib::Raw::Z_OK;
say $orig-buf.subbuf(0, $orig-size[0]).decode; # test
=end code

=head1 AUTHORS AND MAINTAINERS

